      "problem": "Which of the following plots is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except the points where the function is undefined: $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…$\n\n- The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,+\\infty ).$\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi .$\n\n- It has no zeros and no global extrema.\n\n- The branches of the function alternate between positive and negative, with a positive branch for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$\n\n- The graph has vertical asymptotes at the points that are not in the domain: $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…$\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254588/assets/6e302581bbd10dae01387cdff644aa0412feb28f08755113c397bd33c6109557.png)",
